<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n6968" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀναμάρτ-ητος</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ον</span>,
			<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>making no mistake, unerring,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				X.
				<u>Cyr.</u>
				8.7.22
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Pl.
				<u>R.</u>
				339b
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b> in moral
			sense, <i>blameless,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Hp.
				<u>Fract.</u>
				16
			</span></i> (
				Comp.
			), cf. <i><span class="en">
				Antipho
				3.2.10
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Men.
				<u>Epit.</u>
				487
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Phld.
				<u>Sto.Herc.</u>
				339.17
			</span></i>; <i>sinless,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Ev.Jo.
				8.7
			</span></i>, cf. Aristeas <i><span class="en">
				252
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Muson.
				<u>Fr.</u>
				2p.6H.
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀ. πολιτεία</span> a
				<i>faultless</i> form of government, <i><span class="en">
				Arist.
				<u>Pol.</u>
				1275b2
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀ. πρός τινα</span>
			<i>having done no wrong to</i> a person, <i><span class="en">
				Hdt.
				1.117
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τινί</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					5.39
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀ. τινός</span>
			<i>guiltless of</i> a thing, <i><span class="en">
				1.155
			</span></i>: <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὸ -ητότατον,</span>
			
				=
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀναμαρτησία</span>
			, <i><span class="en">
				X.
				<u>Ages.</u>
				6.7
			</span></i>, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Pl.
				<u>R.</u>
				477e
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πρὸς τὸ ἀ.</span>”
				<i>to preserve from error,</i>
				 <i><span class="en">
					Arist.
					<u>EN</u>
					1155a13
				</span></i>
			. Adv.
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">-τως</span>”
				<i>without fail, unerringly,</i>
				 <i><span class="en">
					X.
					<u>Mem.</u>
					2.8.5
				</span></i>
			; <i>without making a mistake,</i> Ps.-<i><span class="en">
				Alex.
			</span></i>Aphr. <i><span class="en">
				<u>in SE</u>
				15.33
			</span></i>; <i>inoffensively,</i> [<i><span class="en">
				D.
			</span></i>]<i><span class="en">
				61.21
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b> of things,
				<i>not done by fault, done unavoidably,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">συμφορά</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Antipho
					3.2.11
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<i>unfailing,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Dion.Byz.
				17
			</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
